      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "mirror_self_reflection_concept",
      "label": "Mirror Self-Reflection Concept",
      "description": "The use of a mirror to depict dual self-portraits is a visual metaphor for internal conflict or self-perception. In this meme, the mirror represents the contrast between how the person perceives themselves (or how they are perceived by others) and how they choose to respond to criticism. This concept is rooted in psychology and self-image theory.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
